= Systems biology =

== Overview ==
'''Systems biology''' studies biological processes as interacting, dynamic systems by integrating experimental measurements with computational, mathematical, or network models.

Instead of isolating one component only, systems biology examines interactions among genes, proteins, metabolites, cells, tissues, organisms, and environments across scales. Feedback, regulation, network structure, and dynamic response are common concerns.

Systems biology is not defined by making a network diagram. Models can include differential equations, stochastic processes, constraint-based models, agent-based models, statistical networks, and multiscale approaches, each suited to different questions.

A systems model remains a scientific model: its boundary, parameters, observability, validation data, uncertainty, and perturbation tests determine what conclusions are justified.

== Boundaries ==
* systems biology ≠ network diagram
* systems biology ≠ systems science applied only metaphorically
* large biological dataset ≠ systems-level explanation

